# wave 59 §P — the operator's own Keiga / Hinder / Remand situation (AD4's
# design boards), real Forge, both screens. Seat 0 (human, alice) has an
# uncontested Main Phase 1, Keiga, the Tide Star (ManaCost 5 U) and Remand
# (ManaCost 1 U) in hand, and 8 untapped Islands — 6 for Keiga, 2 held back
# for Remand so she can cast it a second time while Keiga is still on the
# stack from her first cast. Seat 1 (ai, bob) holds Hinder (ManaCost 1 U U)
# and exactly 3 untapped Islands — enough to pay it once, with nothing left
# over, so Forge's own actionable set reads empty for him once he has cast it
# (no partial mana sitting around to make a later priority stop ambiguous).
# Neither Keiga nor Hinder nor Remand needs a BATTLEFIELD target — Keiga's
# own ability is a death trigger, not an ETB, so casting it opens no target
# ask at all; Hinder and Remand each target a SPELL on the stack, chosen
# through Forge's own `getChoices` (single legal choice auto-answers; two
# legal choices, once Hinder and Keiga are both up, do not — the spec picks
# Hinder by name).
#
# Each hand also carries two copies of Quicken (ManaCost U, Instant, no target —
# an INSTANT on purpose: a creature is sorcery-speed only and Forge refuses
# to offer one while anything is on the stack, which a 0-cost-creature
# version of this file learned the hard way) —
# the chain-reaction measurement's own four-item stack (§P item 2): alice,
# bob, alice, bob each cast one Quicken in turn (nobody is ever left holding
# priority for a reason other than Forge's own "the caster does not stop on
# its own spell" rule — `scenarios/README.md`'s own note on `two-spells.state`
# is why these are FOUR INDEPENDENT casts, never one seat casting two in a
# row). Paid for out of the SAME Islands the Keiga/Hinder/Remand exchange
# uses (a separate test, a separate match, never both at once) — the chain
# test passes priority itself, by an explicit click, rather than leaning on
# Forge's own auto-pass-when-nothing-left-to-do, so it does not matter that
# Keiga/Remand/Hinder are still technically affordable afterward.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=Keiga, the Tide Star;Remand;Quicken;Quicken
humanbattlefield=Island;Island;Island;Island;Island;Island;Island;Island
humanlibrary=Island;Island;Island;Island;Island;Island
humangraveyard=
aihand=Hinder;Quicken;Quicken
aibattlefield=Island;Island;Island
ailibrary=Island;Island;Island;Island;Island;Island
aigraveyard=
